.TH "PKI \-\-BUNDLE" 1 "2026-09-14" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" "strongSwan"
.
.SH "NAME"
.
pki \-\-bundle \- Provides PEM certificate bundle functions
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.
.SY pki\ \-\-bundle
.BR \-\-list
.OP \-\-in file
.OP \-\-debug level
.YS
.
.SY pki\ \-\-bundle
.BI \-\-export\~ index
.OP \-\-in file
.OP \-\-outform encoding
.OP \-\-debug level
.YS
.
.SY pki\ \-\-bundle
.BI \-\-options\~ file
.YS
.
.SY "pki \-\-bundle"
.B \-h
|
.B \-\-help
.YS
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.
This sub-command of
.BR pki (1)
provides functions to work with PEM-encoded certificate bundle.
.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.
.TP
.B "\-h, \-\-help"
Print usage information with a summary of the available options.
.TP
.BI "\-v, \-\-debug " level
Set debug level, default: 1.
.TP
.BI "\-+, \-\-options " file
Read command line options from \fIfile\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-l, \-\-list"
List certificates contained in a PEM-encoded certificate bundle.
.TP
.BI "\-e, \-\-export " index
Export the certificate with the given \fIindex\fR.  Use \fI\-\-list\fR to
determine the index of certificates.
.TP
.BI "\-f, \-\-outform " encoding
Encoding of the exported credential. Either \fIder\fR (ASN.1 DER) or
\fIpem\fR (Base64 PEM), defaults to \fIder\fR.
.TP
.BI "\-i, \-\-in " file
PEM input file. If not given the input is read from \fISTDIN\fR.
.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.
.BR pki (1)
